Don't delete the alock files you backed up yet! check to see what df
says about that partition. If it says 0 bytes free and the amount used <
the total on the partition, then you're in luck. Delete/move files until
the amount free is >0 say 5-10 meg and *then* do a recover, chown thre
resulting save file to games/games and then try it then. Nethack will
crash if the *available* disk space is reported as 0 with linux *not*
when the drive is full. You can see how that would matter from what I
said above. The files are properly written (unless space *is* *very*
close to 0). 

One last time *make* *sure* that the space *available* on the partition
is > 0 when you run recover and nethack and keep it above 0 otherwise
nethack won't run - in fact a game will crash if you change levels when
the space becomes 0. 


Try cleaning out your /tmp directory if it's on the same partition.
That's harmless and the most likely cause for kernels after 2.4. 

